agent-transcripts/
terminals/
mcps/
/.cursor
# Editor + tooling metadata (PostHog wizard, Claude session artifacts).
# Not source — local-only tooling state. Treat like .vscode / .idea.
#
# ONE EXCEPTION: `.claude/settings.json` is the repo-wide Claude Code
# permission deny-list (docs/SECURITY-HARDENING.md step 4b). It is a security
# control, so it has to be tracked and present in every CI checkout — the old
# blanket `.claude/` rule made `git add` skip it *silently* (`git add -A` no-ops,
# `git add .claude/settings.json` exits 1), which is the worst possible failure
# mode for a control someone believes they installed.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an *excluded directory* — once a parent
# directory is ignored, git never descends into it, so a bare `!.claude/settings.json`
# under `.claude/` would do nothing. The rule therefore has to exclude the
# directory's *contents* (`.claude/*`) and then negate the one file.
# Do not collapse this back to `.claude/`.
#
# Verify. `git check-ignore` exit codes are inverted from the intuition, and
# `-v` additionally changes behaviour once the file is tracked, so use both:
#
#   git check-ignore .claude/settings.json
#     -> no output, exit 1 = NOT ignored. This is the state we want, and it
#        reads the same whether the file is tracked, untracked or absent.
#
#   git check-ignore --no-index -v .claude/settings.json
#     -> ".gitignore:<n>:!.claude/settings.json", exit 0. The leading `!` is the
#        point: -v reports the matching RULE, and a negation rule means the path
#        is re-included. Do not read that exit 0 as "still ignored".
#        (--no-index matters: without it, -v goes quiet and exits 1 once the
#        file is tracked, because git skips ignore rules for tracked paths.)
#
#   git ls-files .claude/   -> must list .claude/settings.json once committed.
#                              This is the check that actually proves the point:
#                              it asks the index, not the rules.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
/.pdf_review
# Regenerable SEO job output. Audited baseline snapshots that belong in the
# repository live under docs/seo instead.
/artifacts/seo/
# `/scripts` removed: that directory holds tracked utility scripts
# (schedule-all-broadcasts, schedule-daily-campaign, preview-daily-campaign,
# count-audience-contacts, polish-emails). Ignoring the whole directory
# silently blocked new scripts from being added to the deploy. If a
# specific script in there needs to stay local, ignore it by exact
# filename instead of the parent folder.


# lock files (optional - depends on your team)
/package-lock.json
/yarn.lock
/pnpm-lock.yaml
